rrent.","checks":"Check the axis load meter at rest and while moving; check way lubrication; confirm the brake releases (support vertical axes first).","repairable":"Often mechanical; motor or amplifier repair when current is high with no load.","service":"Servo motor repair; servo amplifier repair"},{"code":"SV0437","slug":"sv0437","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Converter: input circuit overcurrent","area":"Power supply (PSM)","also":"PSM display 1; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 437"},{"code":"SV0438","slug":"sv0438","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: motor current alarm","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display b / C / d; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 438","meaning":"The servo amplifier detected abnormal motor current. Shown on the amplifier as b, c or d for the L, M or N axis.","symptoms":"Alarm at enable or during acceleration.","causes":"Motor winding short or ground fault; damaged power cable; wrong servo parameters; faulty current detection in the amplifier.","checks":"Megger the motor and cable; compare phase-to-phase winding resistance; check that servo parameters match the motor.","repairable":"Yes, when the amplifier or motor is at fault.","service":"Servo amplifier repair; servo motor repair"},{"code":"SV0439","slug":"sv0439","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Converter: DC link overvoltage","area":"Power supply (PSM)","also":"PSM display 7; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 439"},{"code":"SV0440","slug":"sv0440","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Converter: Excessive deceleration power","area":"Power supply (PSM)","also":"PSM display H; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 440"},{"code":"SV0441","slug":"sv0441","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Current offset error","area":"CNC servo monitoring","also":"16i/18i/21i/0i: 441"},{"code":"SV0442","slug":"sv0442","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Converter: DC link precharge failure","area":"Power supply (PSM)","also":"PSM display 5; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 442","meaning":"The power supply (PSM) could not charge the DC link at power-on. Shown on the PSM as 5.","symptoms":"The machine will not reach ready after switch-on.","causes":"Short on the DC link from a failed servo or spindle amplifier; failed PSM precharge circuit; failed DC link capacitor.","checks":"With power off, disconnect the DC link busbars from each amplifier in turn to find a short.","repairable":"Yes: precharge and DC link faults are repairable.","service":"Power supply (PSM) repair; servo amplifier repair"},{"code":"SV0443","slug":"sv0443","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Converter: cooling fan stopped","area":"Power supply (PSM)","also":"PSM display 2; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 443","meaning":"The cooling fan in the power supply (PSM) stopped. Shown on the PSM as 2.","symptoms":"Alarm at power-on or after running; the fan is silent or slow.","causes":"Failed fan motor; fan clogged with oil mist or dust; fan connector fault.","checks":"Check whether the fan spins and is clean.","repairable":"Yes: fan replacement is a quick repair.","service":"Power supply (PSM) repair; cooling fan replacement"},{"code":"SV0444","slug":"sv0444","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: internal cooling fan stopped","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display 1; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 444","meaning":"The internal cooling fan in the servo amplifier (SVM) stopped. Shown on the SVM as 1.","symptoms":"Alarm at power-on or after running; the fan is silent or slow.","causes":"Failed fan; fan clogged with oil mist or dust; fan connector fault.","checks":"Check whether the fan spins and is clean.","repairable":"Yes: fan replacement is a quick repair.","service":"Servo amplifier repair; cooling fan replacement"},{"code":"SV0445","slug":"sv0445","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Soft disconnection alarm","area":"Pulsecoder (encoder) / feedback","also":"16i/18i/21i/0i: 445"},{"code":"SV0447","slug":"sv0447","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Hard disconnection alarm (separate)","area":"Pulsecoder (encoder) / feedback","also":"16i/18i/21i/0i: 447"},{"code":"SV0448","slug":"sv0448","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Feedback mismatch alarm","area":"CNC servo monitoring","also":"16i/18i/21i/0i: 448"},{"code":"SV0449","slug":"sv0449","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: IPM alarm","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display 8. / 9. / A.; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 449","meaning":"The IPM (power module) in the servo amplifier (SVM) shut itself down for protection. Shown on the amplifier as 8., 9. or A. for the L, M or N axis.","symptoms":"Alarm on enable or during motion; often returns immediately after reset.","causes":"Short or ground fault in the motor or motor cable; failed IPM; coolant or oil contamination inside the amplifier; motor winding breakdown.","checks":"Megger the motor and power cable to ground with the cable disconnected from the amplifier; inspect the amplifier for contamination.","repairable":"Yes: IPM replacement is one of our most common Fanuc amplifier repairs.","service":"Servo amplifier repair; servo motor repair"},{"code":"SV0453","slug":"sv0453","type":"Servo alarm","name":"α Pulsecoder soft disconnection","area":"Pulsecoder (encoder) / feedback","also":"16i/18i/21i/0i: 453"},{"code":"SV0600","slug":"sv0600","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: DC link current alarm","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display 8; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 600"},{"code":"SV0601","slug":"sv0601","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: cooling fan stopped of the radiator","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display F; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 601"},{"code":"SV0602","slug":"sv0602","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: overheat","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display 6; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 602"},{"code":"SV0603","slug":"sv0603","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Inverter: IPM alarm (OH)","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display 8. / 9. / A.; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 603"},{"code":"SV0604","slug":"sv0604","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Communication error between amplifiers","area":"Servo amplifier (SVM)","also":"SVM display P; 16i/18i/21i/0i: 604"},{"code":"SV0605","slug":"sv0605","type":"Servo alarm","name":"Co